Critical Rules — Must not be broken in any STEP
Zero-Mutation: The original text extracted from the source (Word/PDF) must not be altered at all during processing. Any transformation must be verified via a SHA-256 hash (canonical NFC-normalized) before and after.

COM Threading: All interactions with InDesign COM must occur exclusively inside a single worker thread named COMWorker(QThread). Never on the UI thread. Never pass live COM objects (Document, Page, TextFrame, etc.) between threads — only file paths, primitives, and Qt Signals.

STA Lifecycle: pythoncom.CoInitialize() at the beginning of run(), and pythoncom.CoUninitialize() inside a finally block is mandatory.

Smart Text Reflow stays enabled (not disabled) — The correct solution for the overflow issue is manual story threading via a label on the body frame + .override(), not disabling reflow.

Fail-Fast: Upon any breach of text integrity, halt and display an error — do not proceed silently (no silent fallback).

